.TH QORE-APP-SCHEMAS 1 "September 2026" "Qore" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
qore-app-schemas \- retrieve and qualify private application schemas
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B qore-app-schemas
.RB [ --cache-dir " DIR"]
.I COMMAND
.SH DESCRIPTION
Manages independent schema snapshots for Freshdesk, Magento, Mailchimp,
NetSuite, Pipedrive, Trello, Zendesk and Zoom. Documents are obtained directly
from declared upstream sources or imported locally. Every candidate must match
the installed catalogue's compatibility fingerprints and pass installed Qore
action qualification before activation. A failed candidate preserves the
previous selection. No download occurs during package builds, installation,
or application startup.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B list
Show source URLs and instructions for apps requiring imports.
.TP
.B update APP [APP ...]
Download and qualify selected public schemas. Failures are reported separately.
.TP
.B update --all
Attempt all declared public downloads and print instructions for import-only
apps. This does not configure apps requiring imports. A failed download or
qualification returns a nonzero exit status.
.TP
.B import APP FILE
Import a compatible Swagger 2.0 or OpenAPI 3.0 JSON document.
.TP
.B fetch-netsuite ACCOUNT TOKEN_FILE
Fetch account metadata using an OAuth bearer token from an owner-only regular
file (mode 600). Credentials are never passed as command arguments, redirected,
or stored in the snapshot. Customized or incompatible exports are rejected.
.TP
.B status [APP]
Print one active snapshot path or the JSON map of configured apps.
.TP
.B rollback APP [DIGEST]
Requalify and activate the previous or specified snapshot.
.TP
.B run -- COMMAND [ARGS]
Run an application with its configured snapshot map pinned. Unconfigured apps
retain their connection scheme and OAuth2 metadata. Their actions report
APP-SCHEMAS-UNAVAILABLE with setup instructions until a snapshot is available.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B QORE_APP_SCHEMA_SNAPSHOTS
JSON object mapping app IDs to absolute immutable snapshot directories.
Use the output of status for service configuration. In Qorus, set this in
qorus-core's service or container environment so TypeScript workers and proxy
children inherit it. Setting it only in an operator shell or the IDE is insufficient.
Snapshot paths must be readable by the service account at the same absolute
paths in child containers. Use --cache-dir consistently across service accounts.
.PP
Failed selections are retryable in the same process after its configuration or
missing files are corrected. Changing a shell or service configuration does not
change a running process's environment, so normally restart qorus-core to apply it.
After the first successful selection the process pins that snapshot; switching
to a different snapshot always requires a restart. The update command changes
the cache selection, not the running process. Relative paths and symlink aliases
are rejected.
.PP
Install the Qore module and JS dist from the same source revision, including any
copy in $OMQ_DIR/qlib. A catalogue protocol mismatch names both versions and
reports TYPESCRIPT-CATALOGUE-PROTOCOL-ERROR. Check QORE_TYPESCRIPT_MASTER_ACTION_SCRIPT
and QORE_MODULE_DIR.
.TP
.B XDG_CACHE_HOME
Cache root; defaults to ~/.cache. App snapshots live under qore/app-schemas.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
qore-app-schemas update magento mailchimp
qore-app-schemas import freshdesk /path/to/export.json
qore-app-schemas run -- qore my-application.q
qore-hubspot-schemas run -- qore-app-schemas run -- COMMAND
.fi
.SH NOTES
An upstream API generation change may require a matching catalogue update.
The updater never approves new fingerprints itself. See README.Debian and
the provider's terms before obtaining documents. Import-only apps do not
silently fall back to bundled documents.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR qore-hubspot-schemas (1)
